== 2. local solvability at every prime p <= 211 (Hensel), Weil above
  p = 2: n with a unit-coordinate solution mod 32 (hence 2-adically representable): all except exactly n = 5 mod 8
  p = 3: x^4 = 1 mod (1 - w) for units, so any n has a unit-coordinate solution mod (1 - w) (take n mod 3 or 3 units), and 4x^3 is a unit there: no 3-adic obstruction
  every n in 1..200 has a nonsingular solution mod p (hence is p-adically representable) for all primes 5 <= p <= 211: True
  p > 211: p does not divide n <= 200, the residue field has q >= p > 81^(2/3) = 18.7 elements, and Weil (N >= q^3 - 81 q^(3/2) > 0 for c != 0) gives a solution, which lifts (4x^3 a unit). [For p | n one would use x1^4 + x2^4 + x3^4 = -1, N >= q^2 - 27 q > 0 for q > 27; not needed above 211.]
  archimedean place: Z[w] (x) R = C, no condition
